==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|zickin|zickīn|female kid|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|tikk-īn-|lang=gem-pro}} (compare Old English {{term|ticcen||kid|lang=ang}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{recons|digós||goat|lang=ine-pro}}, genitive of {{recons|díks|lang=ine-pro}}. More at {{l|de|Ziege}}.

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f||Zicken}}
# [[she-goat]], [[nanny goat]]
# [[bitch]] (arrogant woman)

